President Vladimir Putin's words  signaled a new phase of Russia's war in  Ukraine formalizing what he said was  pre-existing military rule in the  annexed regions of Donetsk luhansk  zapore and her son  I signed a decree on the introduction of  Martial law in these four entities of  the Russian Federation it will be  immediately sent to the Federation  Council for approval  Putin also established local Army  Headquarters and a special coordination  Council in the regions under the  leadership of Russia's prime minister  the decree comes among threats of a new  offensive by the Ukrainian armed forces  and an extensive Russian operation to  move tens of thousands of people from  Herson to the Southern Bank of the  Junipero River  they are told it's to protect them from  Ukrainian shelling  there is a continuing evacuation to give  the peaceful population a chance to  cross To the Left Bank of the kherson  region the entrance to the region is  closed for civilian for seven days  through all directions and all Crossings  under Russian law the decree means the  evacuations can now become compulsory  and the authorities can impose any  measures they see fit including  restricting public life or forcing  people to join the Army civilian  Industries and services can also be used  for military purposes  the new commander of the Russian  operation in Ukraine Sergey sorovicin  acknowledged the situation is difficult  for Russian forces and said what he  called painful measures might be  required the Russian army has suffered  major defeats in eastern and southern  Ukraine since early September it's not  clear what Undeclared measures the new  phase might include in terms of tactics  or types of weapons that Russia might  deploy to reverse those defeats Muhammad  al-jazeera Moscow
 

